<title>FRANCE: MATIF financial futures volume rose in December.</title>
<headline>MATIF financial futures volume rose in December.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in December rose 6.6 percent from the previous month and fell 4.8 percent compared to December 1996, Matif said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	5.21 bln   +6.6 pct    -4.8 pct   837,248</p>
<p>  Financial futures 4.36 bln   +8.7 pct    -0.5 pct   409,666</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 2.97 bln  +18.9 pct   +11.3 pct   134,688</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  854,118  -16.2 pct   -28.2 pct   219,524</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 497,224   +9.5 pct    +5.1 pct    49,385</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	39,249   -3.1 pct   -23.5 pct     6,069</p>
<p>  Financial options  845,242   -3.2 pct   -22.2 pct   427,582</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond  677,415   +4.2 pct    +1.6 pct   238,876</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  158,773  -28.4 pct   -60.4 pct   185,331</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
